{"created": "2026-08-18T10:25:46.511147+00:00", "modified": "2026-08-18T10:25:50.518988+00:00", "id": 21993240, "conceptrecid": "17721007", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21993240", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.17721007", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21993240", "metadata": {"title": "Hydrodynamic Stability Hypothesis: Re-grounding Quantum Mechanics in Classical Measure Theory", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21993240", "publication_date": "2026-08-18", "description": "<p>v1.0 of this work identified a &ldquo;chronological fallacy&rdquo; at the heart of quantum foundations, claiming that the axiomatization of quantum mechanics by von Neumann (1932) predated the rigorous formulation of classical probability by Kolmogorov (1933). That historical claim is withdrawn in v1.1: measure-theoretic probability was established by Borel (1909) and Wiener (1923), before Kolmogorov&rsquo;s 1933 synthesis (see ERRATA.md). To resolve the &ldquo;spectral divergence&rdquo; between the continuous ontology of hydrodynamic quantum models and the discrete phenomenology of spectroscopy, the hydrodynamic stability hypothesis is proposed. By synthesizing Madelung hydrodynamics, Radon-Nikod&yacute;m measure theory, and dynamical systems theory, it is demonstrated that &ldquo;quantization&rdquo; is not an intrinsic property of the operator algebra, but an emergent dynamical stability phenomenon triggered by the measurement interaction. Eigenstates of the Hamiltonian act as basins of attraction for the probability fluid, making the &ldquo;quantum jump&rdquo; a continuous, deterministic relaxation process. This framework restores a Kolmogorovian probability structure to quantum mechanics, resolving the measurement problem without abandoning local realism or invoking discontinuous collapse.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Quni-Gudzinas, Rowan Brad", "affiliation": "QNFO", "orcid": "0009-0002-4317-5604"}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.2139/ssrn.5809662", "relation": "isIdenticalTo", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "1.1.2", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "communities": [{"id": "qnfo"}, {"id": "ultrametric"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 3, "is_last": false, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "17721007"}}]}, "notes": "v1.1.0 (2026-08-18): ERRATA.md added \u2014 the v1.0 'chronological fallacy' historical premise (von Neumann 1932 vs Kolmogorov 1933) is withdrawn as historically inaccurate (Borel 1909, Wiener 1923 predate Kolmogorov's synthesis).\n\nv1.1.1 (2026-08-18): record-level abstract corrected \u2014 the withdrawn 1932/1933 chronology claim is now stated as withdrawn in the abstract itself (the file abstract and ERRATA.md were corrected in v1.1.0; this version aligns the harvested record abstract).\n\nv1.1.2 (2026-08-18): record-level abstract corrected (exact-string replacement) \u2014 the withdrawn 1932/1933 chronology claim is now stated as withdrawn in the abstract itself. v1.1.1 (21993213) was a metadata pass that did not alter the description; this version completes the fix."}, "title": "Hydrodynamic Stability Hypothesis: Re-grounding Quantum Mechanics in Classical Measure Theory", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21993240", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21993240", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21993240?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21993240", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21993240", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21993240", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21993240/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/17721007", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/17721007", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17721007", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.17721007", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21993240/manifest", "self_iiif_